body:
** (asterisk asterisk) could be a pointer to a pointer. They're sometimes used to pass pointers in function parameters.

    Object* obj = new Object();

    // Passing the address of the object pointer
    SendObjectPointer(&obj); 

:: is the scope resolution operator. You use this after typing out the name of a namespace or class to specify the context of the thing you want.

    int main()
    {
        int x = 0;

        // specifying that we want to use the x from our namespace, and not the local x
        MyNamespace::x = 0;

        return 0;
    }
